From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:33:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] pack_app: the game's name in each of its languages
 (DMTitleNames)

The Mac app's bundle name is the first non-empty title of control.nacp,
usually American English, so a front end in another language shows an
English (or Korean) name for a game whose control data has a name in
that language. nacp.names() reads every language's title (plain or
compressed title area, entries that are not printable UTF-8 left out),
and pack_app.py --control writes them into Info.plist as DMTitleNames,
keyed by the codes of nacp.LANGUAGES. The NSP script passes the control
data that lists the game's languages. The control data is part of the
app's reuse key, and nacp.py of its sources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Mac front ends show the game's name in their own language (DMTitleNames from control.nacp)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#895

